vsinpu: leave standalone quantize to the cpu on a733

Standalone QuantizeLinear is built as a TIM-VX DataConvert from float. On the
A733 VIP9000 a DataConvert with float32 or float16 input fails to initialize
(vivante.nn.tensorcopy, status -1), so every model with a float input failed to
verify. uint8 input works because the driver runs it on an NN core; float input
can only use the shader tensorcopy, which fails for every type on this chip
(VIV_VX_DISABLE_TP_NN=1 breaks uint8->float too), why is not known.
DequantizeLinear (uint8->float) works and stays on the npu. QuantizeLinear that
belongs to a QDQ node unit is not affected.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [A733 hardware specific]

--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/vsinpu/builders/impl/quantize_op_builder.h
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/vsinpu/builders/impl/quantize_op_builder.h
@@ -40,27 +40,10 @@
     zero_point_tensor = 2
   };
 
